@startuml flow-provider-listing
!theme plain
title ParkEase BD: Flow Diagram - How a Provider Adds a Parking Space for Rent

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FFF3E0
  BorderColor #E65100
  DiamondBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
}
skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #9E9E9E
}

|Provider|
start
:Register as Provider and verify email;
:Add Property (name, public area,
approximate and exact address);
:Pick the location on the map and
add access and parking rules;
:Upload property photos and
submit for verification;

|System|
:Encrypt exact address, check for
duplicate properties, set status
**PENDING / INACTIVE**;

|Admin|
:Review property: identity, map
location, photos, Provider;
if (Property acceptable?) then (yes)
  :Approve property;
  |System|
  :Set **VERIFIED / ACTIVE**;
else (no)
  |Admin|
  :Reject with a reason;
  |Provider|
  :Edit the property and resubmit;
  stop
endif

|Provider|
:Add parking resource(s): a single fixed space,
bulk spaces (A-01..A-20), or a shared pool,
with vehicle types, size limits and facilities;
:Claim a Parking Right for the resource
(ownership, lease or authorization) and
attach supporting documents;

|Admin|
if (Right proven?) then (yes)
  :Verify the Parking Right;
else (no)
  :Reject, or mark as disputed;
  |Provider|
  :Edit the pending claim and resubmit;
  stop
endif

|Provider|
:Set the parking resource status to **ACTIVE**;
:Create a listing: title, hourly price,
deposit, minimum and maximum duration,
overtime rule, grace period;
:Set weekly availability (tick each open day,
set time ranges) and any date exceptions;
:Activate the listing;

|System|
if (Property VERIFIED and ACTIVE, resource ACTIVE,\nright VERIFIED and valid, availability set?) then (yes)
  :Listing **ACTIVE**: shown in
  search results and bookable;
else (no)
  :Refuse activation and
  tell the Provider why;
  stop
endif

|Provider|
:Optionally add Guards (create or invite,
Guard accepts, Provider assigns a shift)
and invite a Manager with scoped permissions;
stop

@enduml
